          "verdict": "drift flatters",
          "explanation": "The envelope's support bound. 0.439 is today's live value, recomputed daily against a trend that keeps drifting as new data arrives. 0.358 is what the bound would be if it had been frozen at the 2022 low, as a stricter rule would demand. The gap between them is how much the drifting trend flatters the 'envelope intact' reading. Feeds ruling D9-g (freeze each cycle's bound?)."
